  "surprise": "P02 follow-up: MUON_WD 0.1 -> 0.3 (30x) on incumbent 070-claude timed out on seed 2 (SIGALRM at TOTAL_SECS=1200 during the final eval, after all four RL rounds, RL-solved 879). Seeds 0/1 finished at 346/313 vs 070's 359/335 (paired -13/-22; two-seed mean 329.5 vs 347), so the 1x/3x/10x trend (316/327/353) broke between 10x and 30x even apart from the timeout; seed 2 would have needed >=400 (no seed has ever scored above 364) for a keep. The timeout is caused by the idea, the preregistered risk, not a bug: totals 1147/1151/>1200 s vs 070's 1048/971/1079, RL rounds summing 647/656/677 s vs 607/533/620 (round 1 took 219/154/218 s vs 164/139/140), and eval ~193/~187/>217 s vs 131-152 s implied by 070's totals, i.e. slower sampling from the higher-decay policy (sample lengths not measured). Pretraining matched predictions: 4743/4771/4754 steps, final val loss 0.0902/0.0948/0.1002 vs 0.0911/0.0913/0.0961 (within the +0.01 band), held-out greedy 0.981/0.975/0.981 vs 0.987/0.987/0.988 (the 069->070 dip continued). RL improved but did not transfer: RL-solved 816/736/879 vs 788/783/838 (above on 2 of 3 seeds, the predicted plasticity signature), round-4 acc 0.496/0.426/0.520 vs 0.464/0.460/0.485, yet dev-transfer >=7 fell on both finished seeds. First weight-norm measurement (handoff spectral norms, seeds 0/1; seed 2 lost with the timeout): qkv 1.1-1.4, fc1 1.2-1.5, proj 0.54-0.75, fc2 0.53-0.69, head 1.67/1.70 (about 2x their orthogonal init, far below the ~1.13 x shape scale / wd ceilings of 3.8-7.5, so Muon updates are mostly not aligned across steps); emb (AdamW) 3.29/3.43. There are no 10x norms to compare, so the plasticity mechanism remains unverified. Next: keep 10x; logging the same norms on the 10x incumbent would give the missing baseline, and anything between 10x and 30x has little timing headroom.",
